PixelSorcery - notices
======================

PixelSorcery statically recompiles Sega Mega Drive / Genesis games into native
programs. It is a hobbyist, non-commercial project. Its code is licensed under
the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (see LICENSE; the code inherited from
genrecomp stays MIT). The games are not part of it and are not covered by that
licence.


1. The games: bring your own, keep them to yourself
---------------------------------------------------

No ROM, and nothing derived from a ROM, is in this repository or its history:
no game code (recompiled C, disassembly), no graphics, sound, level data,
title labels or attract clips, no recordings of play. The repository holds the
tools and the per-title configuration (addresses, seeds, hooks) only.

Everything game-specific is made on the player's machine, from the player's own
ROM dumps, at build or first-run time (games/*/src/recomp/, the launchers'
labels and clips under Application Support/PixelSorcery/, Mega CD images).

A built game - a native port, a launcher app (which bundles the ports), a
compilation disc - contains code translated from the player's ROMs. That code
remains the copyright of its owners (Sega, Disney and the other rights holders
named in each title). Build and play it yourself; do not share, upload or sell
built games, apps or discs.


